    "y": 415.0201721191406,
    "right": 2123.82568359375,
    "bottom": 530.9475708007812,
    "text": "Translator's Preface",
    "score": 0.9967869579792022
  },
  {
    "x": 160.33258056640625,
    "y": 639.9193725585938,
    "right": 2939.4306640625,
    "bottom": 737.2984008789062,
    "text": "In the prolific world of chess literature, books on the middlegame are comparatively",
    "score": 0.9899759540955225
  },
  {
    "x": 169.62722778320312,
    "y": 739.616943359375,
    "right": 2946.401611328125,
    "bottom": 836.9959716796875,
    "text": "rare - and those on planning even rarer. When the author happens to be a Soviet",
    "score": 0.9932941492599777
  },
  {
    "x": 164.9799041748047,
    "y": 843.95166015625,
    "right": 2944.077880859375,
    "bottom": 934.375,
    "text": "champion and honoured trainer, then the publication of such a work as Chess",
    "score": 0.9785003542900086
  },
  {
    "x": 158.00892639160156,
    "y": 941.3306884765625,
    "right": 2021.584716796875,
    "bottom": 1041.0281982421875,
    "text": "Middlegame Planning arouses even greater interest.",
    "score": 0.992637197971344
  },
  {
    "x": 2033.2030029296875,
    "y": 943.6492309570312,
    "right": 2941.75439453125,
    "bottom": 1031.7540283203125,
    "text": "Peter Romanovsky (1892-",
    "score": 0.9994658102159915
  },
  {
    "x": 158.00892639160156,
    "y": 1041.0281982421875,
    "right": 2941.75439453125,
    "bottom": 1138.4072265625,
    "text": "1964) served his chess apprenticeship in pre-Revolutionary Russia during the same",
    "score": 0.998319892971604
  },
  {
    "x": 153.36160278320312,
    "y": 1131.45166015625,
    "right": 2944.077880859375,
    "bottom": 1242.741943359375,
    "text": "period as his personal friend Alexander Alekhine, to whom he was runner-up in",
    "score": 0.9880418924542217
  },
  {
    "x": 160.33258056640625,
    "y": 1240.4234619140625,
    "right": 2941.75439453125,
    "bottom": 1333.1654052734375,
    "text": "the very first Soviet championship of 1920. After Alekhine's subsequent defection",
    "score": 0.9819363782435288
  },
  {
    "x": 162.65625,
    "y": 1344.758056640625,
    "right": 2941.75439453125,
    "bottom": 1428.225830078125,
    "text": "to the West, Romanovsky himself twice won the Soviet title and achieved fine",
    "score": 0.9960265441944725
  },
  {
    "x": 162.65625,
    "y": 1437.5,
    "right": 2944.077880859375,
    "bottom": 1530.241943359375,
    "text": "results ahead of famous grandmasters in the few international tournaments which",
    "score": 0.9980617180655275
  },
  {
    "x": 164.9799041748047,
    "y": 1537.1976318359375,
    "right": 2941.75439453125,
    "bottom": 1629.9395751953125,
    "text": "were held in the USSR during the 2Os and 3Os. He also became closely aquainted",
    "score": 0.9889923922526531
  },
  {
    "x": 164.9799041748047,
    "y": 1639.2137451171875,
    "right": 2939.4306640625,
    "bottom": 1736.5927734375,
    "text": "with those other great world champions, Lasker and Capablanca, who both spent a",
    "score": 0.9888207346578187
  },
  {
    "x": 160.33258056640625,
    "y": 1743.5484619140625,
    "right": 1275.689697265625,
    "bottom": 1824.6976318359375,
    "text": "fair amount of time in Russia.",
    "score": 0.9418895781040192
  },
  {
    "x": 237.0133819580078,
    "y": 1836.2904052734375,
    "right": 2944.077880859375,
    "bottom": 1933.66943359375,
    "text": "After the Second World War, Romanovsky retired from competitive play and",
    "score": 0.9879312093059222
  },
  {
    "x": 164.9799041748047,
    "y": 1940.625,
    "right": 2946.401611328125,
    "bottom": 2031.0484619140625,
    "text": "assumed a major role as a trainer, writer and populariser of chess. He lectured on",
    "score": 0.9848682437001205
  },
  {
    "x": 167.30355834960938,
    "y": 2040.3226318359375,
    "right": 2946.401611328125,
    "bottom": 2130.74609375,
    "text": "the game from 1947-57 at Moscow University, was on the editorial board of the",
    "score": 0.9883699455818573
  },
  {
    "x": 160.33258056640625,
    "y": 2135.383056640625,
    "right": 2948.725341796875,
    "bottom": 2235.080810546875,
    "text": "official Chess in the USSR magazine from its inception, and wrote 16 books. After",
    "score": 0.9967229491398658
  },
  {
    "x": 155.6852569580078,
    "y": 2235.080810546875,
    "right": 2946.401611328125,
    "bottom": 2332.459716796875,
    "text": "his death, many unpublished manuscripts were discovered amongst his archives -",
    "score": 0.9942386349042257
  },
  {
    "x": 169.62722778320312,
    "y": 2339.415283203125,
    "right": 2774.45068359375,
    "bottom": 2432.1572265625,
    "text": "regrettably most of these treasures still remain unpublished to this day.",
    "score": 0.9786189410784473
  },
  {
    "x": 239.3370361328125,
    "y": 2432.1572265625,
    "right": 2948.725341796875,
    "bottom": 2534.17333984375,
    "text": "A cultured man with varied interests, in particular music and literature, he",
    "score": 0.984744352729697
  },
  {
    "x": 158.00892639160156,
    "y": 2531.85498046875,
    "right": 2951.049072265625,
    "bottom": 2636.189697265625,
    "text": "smiled when once asked why he did not put more effort into becoming a",
    "score": 0.9890591899553934
  },
  {
    "x": 164.9799041748047,
    "y": 2638.508056640625,
    "right": 2953.37255859375,
    "bottom": 2733.568603515625,
    "text": "grandmaster - “Oh, because in life there are many attractions which I did not want",
    "score": 0.9870117953637751
  },
  {
    "x": 158.00892639160156,
    "y": 2719.6572265625,
    "right": 697.0982055664062,
    "bottom": 2844.85888671875,
    "text": "to pass by....\"",
    "score": 0.9911751985549927
  },
  {
    "x": 243.98435974121094,
    "y": 2835.584716796875,
    "right": 2941.75439453125,
    "bottom": 2926.008056640625,
    "text": "In the Soviet School of Chess, Kotov and Yudovich write \"Romanovsky is an",
    "score": 0.9914202069583005
  },
  {
    "x": 164.9799041748047,
    "y": 2937.600830078125,
    "right": 2955.6962890625,
    "bottom": 3034.97998046875,
    "text": "artist and seeker. He strives, in his games, to prove or refute one or another",
    "score": 0.9912033669459515
  },
  {
    "x": 167.30355834960938,
    "y": 3034.97998046875,
    "right": 2953.37255859375,
    "bottom": 3132.35888671875,
    "text": "strategic idea, to create interesting and beautiful combinations. His Middlegame is",
    "score": 0.9991764462137797
  },
  {
    "x": 169.62722778320312,
    "y": 3130.040283203125,
    "right": 2948.725341796875,
    "bottom": 3227.41943359375,
    "text": "one of the best books in the world's chess literature; it has served as a guide for",
    "score": 0.9912491433591728
  },
  {
    "x": 169.62722778320312,
    "y": 3239.01220703125,
    "right": 2948.725341796875,
    "bottom": 3331.754150390625,
    "text": "many Soviet masters .... By his day-to-day penetrating analyses of his own games",
    "score": 0.9892715625464916
  },
  {
    "x": 164.9799041748047,
    "y": 3331.754150390625,
    "right": 2932.459716796875,
    "bottom": 3429.133056640625,
    "text": "and the games of others, in which he seeks out unnoticed possibilities,",
    "score": 0.9783719366704914
  },
  {
    "x": 160.33258056640625,
    "y": 3433.770263671875,
    "right": 2944.077880859375,
    "bottom": 3526.51220703125,
    "text": "Romanovsky sets the youth an example of how to work on self-improvement. He",
    "score": 0.9955337484677632
  },
  {
    "x": 169.62722778320312,
    "y": 3542.741943359375,
    "right": 2944.077880859375,
    "bottom": 3626.209716796875,
    "text": "teaches young players not only the fine points of modern technique but the",
    "score": 0.9760889781487955
  },
  {
    "x": 162.65625,
    "y": 3626.209716796875,
    "right": 2193.53564453125,
    "bottom": 3732.863037109375,
    "text": "evolution of chess ideas and the history of the game.\"",
    "score": 0.9972368931328809
  },
  {
    "x": 248.63168334960938,
    "y": 3737.5,
    "right": 2946.401611328125,
    "bottom": 3825.60498046875,
    "text": "Chess Middlegame Planning was published in Moscow 1960. Its originality and",
    "score": 0.9928770144780477
  },
  {
    "x": 160.33258056640625,
    "y": 3825.60498046875,
    "right": 2953.37255859375,
    "bottom": 3932.258056640625,
    "text": "practical value, allied to a colourful literary style, made it an immediate classic. It is",
    "score": 0.9947750786940257
  },
  {
    "x": 169.62722778320312,
    "y": 3927.62109375,
    "right": 2576.939697265625,
    "bottom": 4031.955810546875,
    "text": "now offered to readers for the first time in the English language.",
    "score": 0.9764533322868925
  },
  {
    "x": 2437.52001953125,
    "y": 4133.9716796875,
    "right": 2951.049072265625,
    "bottom": 4226.7138671875,
    "text": "Jimmy  Adams",
    "score": 0.9814122716585795
  },
  {
    "x": 2465.40380859375,
    "y": 4238.306640625,
    "right": 2946.401611328125,
    "bottom": 4317.13720703125,
    "text": "London 1990",
    "score": 0.9745521328665994
